  "body": "## Why\n\nA new install landed on the Providers tab with no indication of what to do first, in what order, or when setup was actually finished.\n\n## What this adds\n\nA **Get Started** view, first in the nav and the landing view on first run. Seven steps, each with a button that switches to the page where the work actually happens — it walks you through the dashboard rather than duplicating it.\n\n| Step | Opens | Green when |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Connect a model provider | Providers | a provider credential exists |\n| Set your fallback model | Model Config | the fallback can actually serve a request |\n| Point Claude Code at FCC | Providers → settings card | that file really says so |\n| Enable web search *(optional)* | Web Search | a search credential exists |\n| Connect messaging *(optional)* | Messaging | the selected platform has its token |\n| Send your first request *(optional)* | Analytics | the request log has a row |\n| Take the tour *(optional)* | Guide | you have opened it |\n\n## Done-ness is derived, not ticked\n\nEvery step's state comes from **actual configuration, server-side**. A step is green because a credential exists — not because someone clicked something. The checklist therefore cannot drift from reality, stays correct when you configure something outside the flow, and goes back to red if you later remove a key. The Claude Code step reuses the same `read_status` the 4.28.0 settings card uses.\n\nSteps derive from `PROVIDER_CATALOG` and `WEBSEARCH_CATALOG`, not a hardcoded list of env var names, so a new provider is picked up automatically.\n\n## A required step that was green for everyone\n\n`MODEL` ships with a template value, so an \"is it non-empty\" check reported **Set your fallback model** as already done on a machine where nothing was configured — a required step pre-satisfied on a fresh install.\n\nIt now asks whether the fallback **can actually serve a request**: the model ref's provider prefix resolves to a provider that has a credential. Keeping the shipped default is still legitimately done once its provider has a key, which is more useful than nagging about a model that already works.\n\n```\nfresh install, empty home:   0 / 3 essential steps, nothing green\nthis machine, keys present:  2 / 3\n```\n\n## Verification — driven in a real browser against a 4.29.0 server\n\n- Lands on Get Started, **2 of 3 essential steps done**, markers matching the server JSON exactly.\n- **Open Guide** → view switches, `POST /admin/api/onboarding {\"visited\":[\"guide\"]}` persists, the step flips `OPTIONAL` → `DONE` on re-render, and progress correctly stays *2 of 3* because it is optional.\n- **Dismiss** → server records `dismissed: true`; a reload lands on Providers instead, while the nav entry remains so it is still reachable.\n- **No §36 regression.** A container-less view once broke *every* settings tab, so this was checked rather than assumed — after adding a second one, all seven views still render: `providers` 2 sections, `model_config` 3, `messaging` 2, `web_search` 1, `guide` and `get_started` static.\n- The Dismiss control sits under the fixed action bar before scrolling but has 105px clearance at full scroll, so it is reachable. Verified with `elementFromPoint` rather than assumed from a click that appeared to succeed.\n\n**Full suite: 3210 passed, 14 failed** — the documented pre-existing baseline (6 PowerShell installer tests, 8 defeated by real API keys in the shell). Run locally with `env -u ENABLE_WEB_SERVER_TOOLS`, which otherwise inflates the count to ~43 on unmodified `main` too.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- `analytics` is done once the request log has any row, so it stays done forever after your first request. That is the intended reading of \"you've seen traffic\", not a live health check.\n- The messaging check knows Telegram and Discord specifically; a future platform needs adding there, unlike the provider checks which are catalog-driven.\n- Auto-open triggers whenever the checklist is incomplete and undismissed, so a user who deliberately skips an essential step keeps landing on it until they dismiss.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
