    "message": "feat(admin): Get Started checklist that walks through the real pages\n\nA new install landed on the Providers tab with no indication of what to do\nfirst, in what order, or when setup was actually finished.\n\nAdds a Get Started view, first in the nav and the landing view on first run.\nSeven steps: connect a provider, set a fallback model, point Claude Code at the\nproxy, then optional web search, messaging, first request and the guide. Each\nstep carries real copy and a button that switches to the page where the work\nhappens, so it walks you through the dashboard rather than duplicating it.\n\nEvery step's done-state is derived server-side from actual configuration, not\nfrom a checkbox the user ticks. A provider step is green because a credential\nexists; the Claude Code step reuses the same read_status the settings card uses.\nThat means the checklist cannot drift from reality, stays correct when something\nis configured outside the flow, and goes back to red if a key is later removed.\n\nThe fallback-model step asks whether the model can actually serve a request --\nits provider prefix resolves to a provider with a credential -- rather than\nwhether MODEL is non-empty. MODEL ships with a template value, so the non-empty\ncheck reported that required step as already done on a machine where nothing was\nconfigured. Keeping the shipped default is still legitimately done once its\nprovider has a key, which is the useful behaviour rather than nagging about a\nmodel that already works.\n\nSteps derive from PROVIDER_CATALOG and WEBSEARCH_CATALOG rather than a hardcoded\nlist of env var names, so a new provider is picked up automatically.\n\nState persists to ~/.fcc/onboarding.json: a dismissed flag and an additive\nvisited list, since the guide step is the only one with no other signal. Reading\nnever raises on a missing or malformed file; writing is atomic.\n\nVerification, driven in a real browser against a 4.29.0 server:\n- Lands on Get Started with 2 of 3 essential steps done, markers matching the\n  server JSON exactly.\n- Open Guide -> view switches, POST persists visited, the step flips OPTIONAL ->\n  DONE on re-render, and progress correctly stays 2 of 3 because it is optional.\n- Dismiss -> server records it, and a reload lands on Providers instead while\n  the nav entry remains, so it is still reachable.\n- All seven views still render their settings after adding a second\n  container-less view: providers 2 sections, model_config 3, messaging 2,\n  web_search 1, guide and get_started static. A container-less view previously\n  broke every settings tab, so this was checked rather than assumed.\n- Fresh-install simulation with an empty home reports 0 of 3 with nothing green;\n  this machine reports 2 of 3. Four regression tests cover the model step,\n  including the template default and an unrecognised custom provider prefix.\n- Full suite: 3210 passed, 14 failed -- the documented pre-existing baseline\n  (6 PowerShell installer tests, 8 defeated by real API keys in the shell).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
